# Copy to .env (start.sh / start.cmd do it for you). Real environment variables win over this file.
# AI setup - pick ONE (or none):
#   1. Recommended: run `ant auth login` once (Anthropic CLI, see the workspace README). No key is stored here.
#   2. Or paste an API key from https://platform.claude.com below.
#   3. Or leave everything empty: the app runs fully OFFLINE from the stored answers (no cost).
# Options 1 and 2 are billed to your Claude Console organization. If both are set, the key wins.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AI_MODE=auto            # auto = Claude when a login or key exists, else offline | claude | mock
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# AI_EFFORT=medium        # low | medium | high
# PORT=8100
# COACH_ALLOW_SAVE=1      # 0 disables "save generated question to the bank"

# --- Phase B: multi-user storage and sign-in (leave empty for single-user local SQLite) ---
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=          # server only, never ship to the browser
# COACH_REVIEWERS=you@example.com   # comma-separated emails or user ids allowed to review submissions
